(2) c = n/ln n and c = n/ln^2 n: competitor in G_n^(alpha) once 1.5*sqrt(K) <= n^alpha
   c=n/ln n    alpha=0.05: competitor in G_n^(alpha) (zero loss, learner L_D >= 1/4) from n ~ 10^16
   c=n/ln n    alpha=0.01: competitor in G_n^(alpha) (zero loss, learner L_D >= 1/4) from n ~ 10^123
   c=n/ln^2 n  alpha=0.05: competitor in G_n^(alpha) (zero loss, learner L_D >= 1/4) from n ~ 10^40
   c=n/ln^2 n  alpha=0.01: competitor in G_n^(alpha) (zero loss, learner L_D >= 1/4) from n ~ 10^282

(3) Lemma 2.1(b) at L=2, d=1: |z(x)-z(x')| <= (kappa/2)|x-x'| on random width-N nets (kappa = their own energy)
   max |z(x)-z(x')| / ((kappa/2)|x-x'|) over 20000 random nets: 0.9622 (must be <= 1)

